Package: xps13-ubuntu-camera
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms, kmod, dracut | initramfs-tools
Recommends: libspa-0.2-libcamera, gstreamer1.0-libcamera, libcamera-tools, v4l-utils
Suggests: xps13-ubuntu-camera-zoom, linux-source
Description: webcam and IR camera support for Dell XPS 13 9340/9350
 Makes the built-in RGB webcam (OmniVision OV02C10) and the IR face-login
 camera (Himax HM1092) work on the Dell XPS 13 9340 (Intel IPU6) and
 XPS 13 9350 (Intel IPU7):
  - HM1092 IR sensor driver (DKMS). Without it the IPU never registers the
    webcam either, because it waits for every sensor listed in ACPI.
  - IPU6 boot-time crash fix (DKMS, built only on IPU6 machines, needs the
    matching linux-source package).
  - initramfs configuration keeping the camera drivers out of the boot image,
    where their undeclared firmware is missing.
  - WirePlumber configuration: hide raw IPU capture nodes, name the cameras
    "Front Camera" and "IR Camera", wait for the camera at login.
  - xps13-camera-check, xps13-camera-setup and xps13-camera-chrome-fix tools.

Package: xps13-ubuntu-camera-zoom
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, xps13-ubuntu-camera (= ${source:Version}),
         v4l2-relayd (>= 0.2.0), v4l2-relayd (<< 0.2.1~)
Description: virtual webcam for Zoom and other V4L2-only apps on Dell XPS 13
 Apps that only use V4L2 directly (such as the Zoom snap) cannot use the
 libcamera-only IPU cameras. This package provides a "Virtual Camera"
 (v4l2loopback) fed from the RGB webcam on demand, using a patched
 v4l2-relayd that fixes frame timestamps and libcamera appsink stalls.
 The real camera is only switched on while an app uses the virtual one.
